---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Local HTTP API"
  description="The currently implemented Veasel Code HTTP endpoints, asynchronous session turns, approval flows, and replayable server-sent events."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / API</p>
    <h1>
      A small local
      <br />
      <em>workspace API.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The versioned HTTP API connects the terminal client to the V server. It
      listens on loopback and currently covers health, capabilities, sessions,
      bounded workspace inspection, reviewed edits and commands, streaming chat,
      per-call MCP approval, and replayable events.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Endpoints</h2>
      <div
        class="provider-table api-table"
        role="table"
        aria-label="Veasel Code API endpoints"
      >
        <div class="provider-table-row provider-table-head" role="row">
          <b role="columnheader">Method</b>
          <b role="columnheader">Path</b>
          <b role="columnheader">Purpose</b>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/health</code>
          <span role="cell">Check the local server.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/capabilities</code>
          <span role="cell">Discover implemented features.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/config/model</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Read or update provider profiles; responses never include API keys.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/config/models?provider=&#123;id&#125;</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Fetch a bounded model list from the configured provider endpoint.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/sessions</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List sessions or create one for an existing directory.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}"}</code>
          <span role="cell">Read session metadata.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/messages"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Page chat history or complete and persist one exchange.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/plugins</code>
          <span role="cell">Discover local plugin and Skill metadata.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/skills</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List standalone discovered Skills across configured roots.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/mcp-servers</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List or upsert configured MCP servers (user/project; optional{" "}
            <code>directory</code> adds project + <code>.mcp.json</code> import;
            <code>mcp.servers.configured</code>).
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">PATCH · DELETE</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/mcp-servers/{name}"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Enable/disable or remove; <code>scope</code> /{" "}
            <code>directory</code> select user or project.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/mcp-credentials</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Named Streamable HTTP credentials (<code>mcp.credentials</code>;
            header names only in responses).
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">DELETE</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/mcp-credentials/{name}"}</code>
          <span role="cell">Remove a named MCP credential.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/mcp-oauth/authorize</code>
          <span role="cell">
            PKCE S256 authorize (<code>mcp.oauth</code>); returns browser URL.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/mcp-oauth/complete</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Finish OAuth with code/state or loopback <code>callback_url</code>.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · PATCH</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/plugins/components</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List or toggle plugin skill/MCP components (
            <code>plugins.components</code>).
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/plugins/links</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List or add local Agent Plugin directory links (no remote fetch).
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">DELETE</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/plugins/links/{name}"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Remove a managed plugin symlink by package name.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/mcp-servers"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List or update per-session trust for MCP servers (
            <code>configured/&lt;name&gt;</code> for user-added servers).
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/mcp-tool-calls"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List recent MCP tool call approvals and outcomes.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/mcp-tool-calls/{call_id}"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">
            Inspect bounded arguments and record review before approval.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/mcp-tool-calls/{call_id}/approve"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">Approve one inspected call for one execution.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/mcp-tool-calls/{call_id}/reject"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">
            Reject a pending call without sending it to the MCP server.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/skills"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List, enable, or disable Skills for one session.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/files"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List up to 500 workspace files; generated directories and symlinks
            are skipped.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/file"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Read one UTF-8 text file up to 512 KB within the selected root.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/search"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Search literal text with bounded file, byte, and result counts.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/map"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Extractive repository map for context selection (also{" "}
            <code>/map</code> in the TUI).
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/edits"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List saved proposals or save a bounded single-file diff for review.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/edits/{edit_id}"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">
            Open a proposal diff; this records that it was reviewed.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/edits/{edit_id}/approve"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">
            Apply the reviewed proposal if the file has not changed.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/edits/{edit_id}/reject"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">Reject a pending proposal without writing.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/commands"}</code>
          <span role="cell">List proposed shell commands for review.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/commands/{command_id}"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">
            Open and inspect the exact command, working directory, and timeout.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/commands/{command_id}/approve"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">
            Run the command after its review is opened and approval recorded.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/commands/{command_id}/reject"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">Reject a proposed command.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/git/worktrees"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List git worktrees (filesystem) or add one (argv-only{" "}
            <code>git worktree</code>).
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">PATCH · DELETE</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/workspace/git/worktrees"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Lock/unlock or remove a worktree by absolute path.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/operations/{operation_id}"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">
            Read durable status for an asynchronous session turn, scoped to its
            session.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">
            {"/v1/sessions/{id}/operations/{operation_id}/cancel"}
          </code>
          <span role="cell">
            Request cancellation of an active session turn.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/operations/{operation_id}/cancel"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Request cancellation of a completion operation.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">POST</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/chat/completions</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Request a provider response without a session.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/events</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Replay events and continue with server-sent events.
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Page session history</h2>
      <p>
        <code>GET /v1/sessions/&#123;id&#125;/messages</code> returns the latest
        100 messages by default, in chronological order. Set <code>limit</code>{" "}
        to a value from 1 to 100 to choose a page size. To fetch an earlier
        page, pass the first message ID from the current page as the exclusive
        <code>before</code> cursor:
      </p>
      <pre><code>curl 'http://127.0.0.1:4097/v1/sessions/SESSION_ID/messages?limit=100&before=101'</code></pre>
      <p>
        An empty array means there are no earlier messages. In the terminal
        client, enter <code>/history older</code> to load and merge the previous
        page while keeping the messages already on screen.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Headless CLI</h2>
      <p>Run a single turn against the same local server and approval rules:</p>
      <pre><code>veasel run --prompt "Explain the request flow in this repository" \
  --workspace . --json</code></pre>
      <p>
        Prefer <code>veasel serve</code> when another client owns the API. Full
        OpenAPI contract:{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/openapi.yaml">
          docs/openapi.yaml
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="callout">
      <strong>Review each effect before approving it.</strong> Session chat can
      let the configured provider request bounded file listing, reads, and
      literal search, or propose one text-file replacement. The normal TUI flow
      opens the saved diff before approval. Veasel checks for file changes since
      review. Shell commands require a separate review of the exact command,
      working directory, and timeout; they may wrap in a platform sandbox when
      available. This loopback API has no application token, so same-user
      processes can call its review and approval routes too. Requested content
      and tool output are sent to your provider.
    </aside>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Resume the event stream</h2>
      <p>
        Events use increasing numeric IDs. Send the last event ID you handled to
        replay newer events after a reconnect. <code>Last-Event-ID</code> must
        be a digit-only non-negative integer (no sign, spaces, or leading zeros
        except <code>0</code>); omit it or send <code>0</code> to start from the
        beginning. Catch-up returns at most 500 events per poll. Quiet streams
        emit <code>event: heartbeat</code> with <code>data: &#123;&#125;</code>{" "}
        about every 15 seconds so clients can detect a live connection without
        inventing session events.
      </p>
      <pre><code>curl -N -H 'Last-Event-ID: 12' \
  http://127.0.0.1:4097/v1/events</code></pre>
      <p>
        Each session event includes its session ID and type. Keep the cursor
        supplied by the server; IDs are created by the local event database.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Wait for an asynchronous turn</h2>
      <p>
        Session message requests are synchronous by default. Send
        <code>Prefer: respond-async</code> to receive <code>202 Accepted</code>
        and a durable operation ID immediately. Follow the replayable event
        stream for <code>assistant.delta</code> and
        <code>session.turn_completed</code>, or query
        <code>/v1/sessions/SESSION_ID/operations/OPERATION_ID</code> after
        reconnecting. A completed turn stores its operation status and chat
        history together. Queued async turns resume after restart (at most 32
        queued rows per session) when request, workspace, and model still
        validate. <code>autonomous:true</code> queued rows resume only when{" "}
        <code>VEASEL_ALLOW_AUTONOMOUS_EXECUTION=1</code> is set — otherwise they
        cancel without claim. If the server restarts after a worker claimed the
        turn but before recording a result, the operation becomes{" "}
        <code>uncertain</code>; Veasel never repeats possible provider or tool
        effects. Operation history management and retention policy remain ahead.
      </p>
      <pre><code>curl -X POST \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -H 'Prefer: respond-async' \
  -d '&#123;&quot;content&quot;:&quot;Inspect this project&quot;&#125;' \
  http://127.0.0.1:4097/v1/sessions/SESSION_ID/messages</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Approve MCP calls individually</h2>
      <p>
        Add user- or project-scoped servers with{" "}
        <code>POST /v1/mcp-servers</code> or{" "}
        <code>/mcp add [user|project]</code> (see the{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>MCP guide</a>). Named credentials and
        OAuth PKCE use <code>/v1/mcp-credentials</code> and{" "}
        <code>/v1/mcp-oauth/*</code>. Per-session trust lets a configured server
        connect; it does not approve tool effects. Each model-requested call
        pauses the active turn. Inspect its exact arguments before approval.
        Rejected calls never reach the server and are not retried.
      </p>
      <pre><code>/mcp calls
/mcp call show CALL_ID
/mcp call approve CALL_ID
/mcp call reject CALL_ID</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Headless CLI companions</h2>
      <p>
        These commands talk to the same loopback API as the TUI (no invented
        scores):
      </p>
      <pre><code>veasel run --prompt "…" --workspace . --json
veasel mcp list
veasel mcp credentials list
veasel mcp oauth authorize &lt;cred&gt; … --listen   # prints URL; no auto browser
veasel skills list [--directory .]
veasel worktrees list
veasel plugins components list</code></pre>
    </div>
    <aside class="callout">
      <strong>Loopback is the boundary.</strong> The API has no application
      token and must not be exposed to a network. Other processes running under
      the same operating-system account can reach session, inspection, and
      approval routes.
    </aside>
    <p class="doc-next">
      <a
        class="text-link"
        href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/openapi.yaml"
      >
        Open the OpenAPI 3.1 document <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/architecture/`}>
        See the request architecture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
